gary meant so much to all of las vegas  and for those of us at 8 news now his  impact immeasurable sasha loftis takes a  look back at the ways he made our  newsroom what it is today  we are back with more of our coverage  his voice could soothe the saddest of  days and his stories shaped our city for  decades the las vegas strip was almost  deserted but for so many here at 8 news  now gary waddell was light laughter and  a symbol of what tv news truly means it  was like he was woven into  the fabric of las vegas his time here in  our newsroom will always be remembered  as he brought his talent sound logic and  unwavering friendship i was so lucky to  have him as a friend i was so lucky to  have him as a colleague it's been nearly  10 years since gary retired and we still  have this box here today 30 years worth  of newspaper clips and photos just a  true testament to the history he  witnessed and the impact he'll have for  so much time to come we showed you the  top 19 stories his former co-anchor and  long time friend paula francis says gary  also spent so much time helping others  and sharing his unparalleled experience  he was so in tune to  current events  to news to history and he really wanted  to impart that to young people gary  always said  find the smartest people you can and  hire them and teach them tv so while  those who knew him are still full of  sorrow  they can also take comfort in the  countless ways he changed the world  one newscast at a time my name is gary  waddell in las vegas  [Music]  sasha loftis 8 news now
 

